--------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Why AGPL-3.0-or-later
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Until BJS-495 the app shipped Strudel and superdough, both AGPL-3.0-or-later,
to every player over the network, and it still carries code derived from them
(section 2). Section 13 of the AGPL obliges whoever runs a modified version for
users over a network to offer those users the corresponding source. This
repository is that offer. The app's "Source & Credits" link (on
the loading screen) points at the tree of the deployed commit; builds that do
not know their commit fall back to the main branch.

The licence applies to the repository as a whole. Content that is not code
(fonts, sample audio, song transcriptions) is a separate question and is
covered below, not by LICENSE.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Strudel and superdough (AGPL-3.0-or-later)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

By the Strudel / TidalCycles community (Alex McLean, Felix Roos and
contributors), https://strudel.cc, https://codeberg.org/uzu/strudel.

The packages are no longer installed or served: BJS-495 removed @strudel/core,
@strudel/mini, @strudel/soundfonts, @strudel/tonal, @strudel/transpiler,
@strudel/webaudio and superdough (versions 1.2.6 and 1.3.0), with the patches
the app applied to superdough and @strudel/soundfonts. Earlier deployed
versions shipped them; their source, patches included, stays in git history.

What the app still carries from them:

- src/data/gmSoundfonts.ts copies the General MIDI name-to-font map from
  @strudel/soundfonts 1.3.0 gm.mjs (as patched), under the same licence.
- src/services/strudelLink.ts reproduces Strudel's code2hash URL encoding so
  "Open in Strudel" opens the app's own code text on strudel.cc.
- The reverb impulse recipe adapted from superdough (section 8; Apache-2.0).

With the packages gone, the licence choice is due for review. Published
snapshots stay AGPL either way.

