--------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. Hilbert scope
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Hilbert scope renderer was influenced by Seeing Music (Creatability,
Google Creative Lab) and adapts the Hamming-window impulse, convolution filter
and compensating delay of its Web Audio adapter, which in turn credits
conundrumer/Audioscope. Both upstream licences are GNU GPL version 3, which
combines with AGPL-3.0. Sources, authors and links are in docs/credits.md.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. Sample packs and soundfonts loaded at runtime
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The app's own loader (src/services/preparedNativeInstrument.ts) fetches these
in the player's browser from the upstream hosts named below. None of the
audio or font data is in this repository or in the built app; EmotiTone does
not redistribute it. The base URLs are in src/audio/sampleSources.ts. Font
files are parsed as data and never evaluated as code. This is not legal
advice.

  Piano (piano.json map, 29 pitches)
    Salamander Grand Piano V3 by Alexander Holm, licensed CC BY 3.0
    (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/). Converted to MP3, single
    velocity layer, by felixroos/dough-samples. Source:
    https://archive.org/details/SalamanderGrandPianoV3
    Fetched from raw.githubusercontent.com/felixroos/dough-samples.

  Orchestra (vcsl.json map, 128 sounds)
    Versilian Community Sample Library (VCSL) by Sam Gossner and
    contributors, CC0 1.0 (https://github.com/sgossner/VCSL). No attribution
    is required; it is given with thanks. Fetched from
    raw.githubusercontent.com/sgossner/VCSL.

  The sample maps (piano.json, vcsl.json)
    By Felix Roos, in felixroos/dough-samples. That repository states no
    licence. The app fetches the maps at runtime and does not copy them.

  General MIDI soundfonts (125 gm_* instruments)
    Converted from SF2 banks by Sergey Surikov in
    https://github.com/surikov/webaudiofontdata (the conversion repository
    is MIT; its owner says the source fonts' licences are unknown, issue #1).
    Fetched from felixroos.github.io/webaudiofontdata. The name-to-font map in
    src/data/gmSoundfonts.ts comes from @strudel/soundfonts (see section 2).
    By each instrument's default (first) font:
    - 20 instruments use FluidR3_GM: MIT licence.
      Copyright (c) 2000-2002, 2008 Frank Wen.
      Mono version: Copyright (c) 2014-16 Michael Cowgill.
      The MIT notice must accompany copies or derivatives of the font.
    - The other 105 instruments use fonts whose licence nobody states:
      JCLive (64), Aspirin (38), Chaos (2) and Acoustic_Guitar (1). They are
      fetched from the upstream host as the app did before; EmotiTone does
      not host or redistribute them. Self-hosting is a separate decision
      (BJS-496).
    Patterns can select other variants of an instrument (".n()"), which
    may come from GeneralUserGS (GeneralUser GS License v2.0, S. Christian
    Collins), FluidR3_GM, or fonts with no stated licence (Aspirin, JCLive,
    Chaos, LesPaul, Stratocaster, SBAWE32, Soul_Ahhs and others).

